{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-62682-r4587304","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Oatmeal Cookies I","sourcePageId":62682,"sourceRevision":"4587304","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:34:51Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Oatmeal%20Cookies%20I&oldid=4587304","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:32.266Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for oatmeal cookies","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using oat","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"89402c1137bb41c600b775d157db9bdd3f8bc05dd108066a8a365a7a458cb476","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{recipesummary|category=Recipes for dessert|servings=20|time=20–25 minutes|difficulty=2\n| Image = [[File:Oatmeal cookies on a plate.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Desserts]]\n\nA tasty '''oatmeal cookie''', just like those you remember.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (180 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Shortening|shortening]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 g) [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (120 g) [[Cookbook:Sugar|white sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (60 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:water|water]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:vanilla|vanilla]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (700 g) [[Cookbook:Oats|rolled oats]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 g) [[Cookbook:flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:salt|salt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]] (optional)\n\n== Special equipment ==\n\n* Electric [[Cookbook:Mixer|mixer]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Using a mixer, [[Cookbook:cream|cream]] together the shortening, brown sugar, white sugar, egg, water and vanilla until light and fluffy (about 10 minutes on high).\n#In a [[Cookbook:Mixing Bowl|mixing bowl]], mix together the oats, flour, baking soda, and salt.\n#Add dry ingredients into wet, mix well using mixer.\n#Stir in raisins if using.\n#Scoop the portions out—this recipe makes 20 cookies, so make 20 portions.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] at [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|350°F]] (180°C) for 8–10 minutes.\n\n==Notes, tips and variations==\n*These taste best when still warm.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for oatmeal cookies|Oatmeal Cookies]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert|Oatmeal Cookies]]\n[[Category:Recipes using oat|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Oatmeal Cookies I","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"¾ cup (180 g) shortening","sourceText":"¾ cup (180 g) shortening","amountText":"¾ cup (180 g) shorteni